                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "df27425a-f5bd-35b4-ad34-22f02f6db45c",
                        "entry_id": "73a97d9a-5565-304c-b173-559ff3da1f39",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The period of the papacy known as the saeculum obscūrum (Latin for “dark age”), and also as the “Rule of the Harlots”, which began with the installation of Pope Sergius III in 904 and lasted for sixty years until the death of Pope John XII in 964, during which time the popes were strongly influenced by the Theophylacti, a powerful and corrupt aristocratic family."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "capitalized",
                            "historical",
                            "often"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed5bc51b-cb0a-425f-af86-6faf82c68ca0",
                                "sense_id": "df27425a-f5bd-35b4-ad34-22f02f6db45c",
                                "text": "Under the pornocracy (government of harlots) in the first half of the 10th century, the Papacy was degraded and all Italy torn by factions."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "29e7523a-9a13-4146-be6a-15983af5efc3",
                                "sense_id": "df27425a-f5bd-35b4-ad34-22f02f6db45c",
                                "text": "Monsters of impurity, avaricious wretches, poisoners, have occupied the papal see. A learned bishop (Maret of the General Council) expresses himself with holy indignation in reference to the frightful enormities of the tenth century. This epoch deserves to be designated under the title of the Pornocracy; that is to say, the government of prostitutes, for Theodora, Marozia, and other ladies of rank at that time, placed on the pontifical throne their paramours and their sons, who were no better than themselves."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
